From: Airtype downstream
Subject: [PATCH] mtmd : plan projector memory without allocating it, and fail allocation gracefully

clip_model_loader::load_tensors allocated the weights buffer even for a no_alloc context, the one
mtmd_get_memory_usage creates to project a projector's memory, and reserve_compute_meta allocated
the compute buffers through ggml_backend_sched_reserve either way. Projecting a GPU projector
therefore briefly held its whole weights and compute buffers on the device, which is the memory the
projection is meant to find out whether there is room for. When there was none, the weights
allocation returned NULL, and ggml_backend_buffer_set_usage aborted the process on GGML_ASSERT
(buffer) rather than letting mtmd_init_from_file return NULL. A real load that runs out of device
memory aborted the same way (https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/21402 reports this
assertion), so a caller had no chance to fall back to the CPU.

For a no_alloc context this points the weights at a zero-size dummy buffer, as
llama_model::load_tensors does for its own no_alloc loads, and measures the compute buffers with
ggml_backend_sched_reserve_size, as llama_context does. The per-device totals are unchanged,
because the weights were already counted tensor by tensor. A failed weights or compute allocation
now throws, which clip_init and mtmd_init_from_file turn into a NULL context.

The compute projection still covers the warmup image, which some projector types cap below their
largest input to avoid out-of-memory errors at warmup (set_warmup_n_tokens(256) for Pixtral and
LightOnOCR), so a full page can need several hundred MiB more at encode time. An encode that cannot
grow its compute buffer already fails with an error rather than aborting.

Upstream report: not yet filed; master as of 95887577 (2026-09-26) still allocates and asserts.

Validated against llama.cpp b11201 on an NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5060 Ti (CUDA 13.3), on top of
0002-mtmd-accumulate-projector-matmuls-in-f32.patch:
- With another process holding most of the device memory, llama-mtmd-cli with Gemma 4 E2B's F16
  projector aborted in ggml_backend_buffer_set_usage before and now reports "load_tensors: unable
  to allocate CUDA0 buffer for the weights" and fails to load the projector.
- mtmd_get_memory_usage reports the same totals for LightOnOCR-2-1B's projector as before (845 MiB
  on the CPU; 845 MiB on CUDA0 plus 8 MiB on the CPU), in 0.23 s instead of 0.43 s, and the
  airtype-desktop-inference-sidecar engine's projector parity and footprint tests still pass.

Refreshed for b12332: models and shared subcontext compute now live in separate sources.
A scoped collector preserves the maximum shared compute projection without changing headers.

